From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domsvoboda <domsvoboda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:51:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winhttp: Never open the HTTP/2 body diagnostics log.

The HTTP/2 transport could write a scan of response bodies to a file
named by XUSER_WINHTTP_BODY_LOG. Its identifier-shaped whitelist can let
token fragments through, so it is not opened in a shared runtime; the
writers stay inert with no file.

Ported from Xodus Nexus unchanged.

Ported-from: https://github.com/domsvoboda/nexus-wine/commit/a58b93d3eb3b6261404776394c92fd93150c860f
Ported: clean
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-wine-gdk-port.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/winhttp/http2.c | 12 ++++--------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winhttp/http2.c b/dlls/winhttp/http2.c
index 01c4e29..bc2cf6f 100644
--- a/dlls/winhttp/http2.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/http2.c
@@ -67,14 +67,10 @@ static HANDLE diag_file;
 
 static void diag_init( void )
 {
-    char path[MAX_PATH];
-    AcquireSRWLockExclusive( &diag_lock );
-    if (!diag_file)
-    {
-        if (GetEnvironmentVariableA( "XUSER_WINHTTP_BODY_LOG", path, MAX_PATH ) && *path)
-            diag_file = CreateFileA( path, GENERIC_WRITE, FILE_SHARE_READ, NULL, OPEN_EXISTING, 0, NULL );
-    }
-    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive( &diag_lock );
+    /* Do not activate the legacy printable-run body scanner in a shared
+     * runtime. Token fragments can match its identifier-shaped whitelist.
+     * Keep transport tracing numerical; schema-aware diagnostics belong in
+     * a separately audited opt-in tool, not the distributed DLL. */
 }
 
 static void diag_emit( char *out, size_t size, size_t *pos, const char *text )
